  "body": "## What changed\n- The machine list and the post list come from a scan of their folders. They no longer come from the fixed `MACHINES` and `BUILTINS` tables.\n- A file in the folder that has no table entry is listed as a file entry. It uses the existing `LoadMachineFile` and `SelectPostFile` commands.\n- A table entry shows only if its file is present. A removed file does not leave an entry.\n- The Refresh buttons scan the folder again (`posting::rescan`). The machine page and the post picker have a Refresh button. The AccessKit names are \"Refresh machine list\" and \"Refresh post list\".\n- A malformed file does not stop the scan. It is listed with its own refusals.\n- A document that needs a missing post or machine is still refused by name (#2319).\n- The MCP machine-name list uses the same scan.\n- The post combo finds the document's post by name (`posting::post_name`) in the scanned list (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/post_pick.rs`). It never indexes past the list. A post whose file is gone shows its own name with \"(file missing)\". The document's post does not change. The Setup Post page shows why the post folder did not read (`FolderScan::problem`).\n- The folder listing is `camcraft_post::data_dir::list_files`. The scan is `camcraft_post::data_scan::scan_folder` (and `FolderScan`). `app` re-exports the two from `posting`.\n- The process cache (`post_scan`, `machine_scan`, `rescan`, `scan_reads`) is in `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`. It binds the scan to the `BUILTINS` and `MACHINES` tables and to the process folders, which are in that file. No new file in `crates/app/src`. No new dependency between our crates.\n\n## Root cause\nThe lists were built from `BUILTINS` and `MACHINES` in `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`. The UI pickers and `machine/library.rs` `builtins()` read those tables. No code read the folder.\n\n## Pinning tests\n`crates/post/tests/folder_scan.rs` (Gate map: `camcraft_post::data_scan`, `camcraft_post::data_dir`):\n- `the_post_list_follows_its_folder`\n- `a_missing_folder_lists_nothing_and_says_why`\n\n`crates/app/tests/folder_lists.rs` (Gate map (#2380): `camcraft_app::posting`, `camcraft_app::machine::library`):\n- `the_machine_list_follows_its_folder`\n- `the_process_lists_read_the_shipped_folders`\n\n`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/structural/folder_refresh.rs` (structural twin: label, role `Button`, enabled state, a press reads the folders again):\n- `the_machine_page_refresh_button_rereads_the_folder`\n- `the_post_picker_refresh_button_rereads_the_folder`\n- `an_empty_post_folder_shows_the_default_post_as_missing` (review fix: the page draws with an empty, unreadable folder; the combo shows the default post as missing; the folder message shows)\n- `a_removed_first_post_is_not_shown_as_another_post` (review fix: the combo's selected text names the post that `script_of` uses)\n\n`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/page_layout.rs`: `layout_page_setup_machine` names \"Refresh machine list\". The post Refresh button is on the same row as \"Load post (.cps)\", thus the post layout test does not name it.\n\n## Readings\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` at 5733391a1 (review fix): 232 steps, 0 failed, 27.9 min. It includes `ui suites: lib`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` at 5733391a1 is clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` at 0679b49f5: 232 steps, 0 failed, 23.1 min. It includes `ui suites: lib`, `post suites: folder_scan` and `app suites: folder_lists`.\n- The quick gate at 384183cf4 was green too: 230 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Screenshots\nHeadless renders (egui_kittest, wgpu, 1280 x 800) of the seeded document with one setup. \"Before\" uses the UI files of `origin/main`. No GUI process was started.\n\nMachine page, before: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/pr-2414/machine-page-before.png?raw=true\nMachine page, after: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/pr-2414/machine-page-after.png?raw=true\nPost page, before: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/pr-2414/post-page-before.png?raw=true\nPost page, after: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/pr-2414/post-page-after.png?raw=true\n\n## Not exercised\n- The real GUI was not started. The screenshots are headless renders.\n- A Refresh with a changed shipped folder was not done in the GUI. The scan tests change scratch folders.\n\n## Decisions\nSee `docs/decisions/2380-folder-scan-lists.md`. A file that was read once and removed later still posts from the cached text until restart.\n\nEffort: medium\nChangelog: Machine and post lists now follow their folders: new files appear, removed files disappear, and Refresh scans again.\n\nFixes #2380\n\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
